# Local values for `wrangler dev` and for the test runner. Copy to .dev.vars, which .gitignore
# already covers, and never commit the copy.
#
# In production these are `wrangler secret put`, not vars: see wrangler.jsonc and README.md.

# The key the api is signing with. Whatever is here must be byte-identical to MEDIA_SIGNING_SECRET
# on the api, including the absence of a trailing newline, or every signed URL 403s. GET /__parity
# on both sides is how you check that without ever printing either value.
MEDIA_SIGNING_SECRET=replace-me-with-a-local-only-value

# The key the api WAS signing with. Set ONLY while a rotation is in flight, and unset again once
# every URL minted under the old key has aged out, which takes at most two hours. Commented out
# here because absent is the normal steady state, and an empty value is treated as absent too.
# MEDIA_SIGNING_SECRET_PREVIOUS=
